{
 "about": "Who does the work, as history had it (decision: history is king). For each geographic region, the share of its people who were dependent (bound tenants, serfs, royal farmers, clients, helots) and enslaved, at points in time; shares between points are interpolated. abolition: the year slavery was abolished in law in the lands of the region (the modern state holding most of it); enslaved share is 0 from then. Approximate, from Scheidel, 'The comparative economics of slavery in the Greco-Roman world' (2008), the Cambridge Economic History of the Greco-Roman World (2007) and general histories; to refine. Our own summary, free for any use.",
